es of Series 1943 F and G bonds for 4% marketable bonds of 1969.\\n8/ Includes exchanges of Series 1950 F and G bonds for 3-7/8% marketable bonds of 1968.\\n9/ Includes exchanges of Series 1951 and 1952 F and G bonds for 3-7/8% marketable bonds of 1971 and 4% marketable bonds of 1980.\\n10/ Represents changes in the amounts of redemptions not yet classified between matured and unmatured issues.\\n* Less than $500,000.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 8, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 29, 92, 53], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"68\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 0, \"type\": \"page_number\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [1329, 2, 1595, 51], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"Treasury Bulletin\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 1, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [571, 68, 1058, 95], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"UNITED STATES SAVINGS NOTES\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 2, \"type\": \"page_header\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [83, 223, 790, 318], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"Sales of United States savings notes began May 1, 1967. The notes are eligible for purchase by individuals with the simultaneous purchase of Series E savings bonds.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 3, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [870, 209, 1597, 355], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"The principal terms and conditions for purchase and redemption and information on investment yields of the savings notes appear in the Treasury Bulletins of March 1967 and June 1968.\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 4, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [538, 432, 1129, 466], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"Table SN-1. - Sales and Redemptions by Periods\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 5, \"type\": \"title\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [734, 493, 970, 515], \"page_id\": 80}], \"content\": \"(In millions of dollars)\", \"description\": null, \"id\": 6, \"type\": \"text\"}, {\"bbox\": [{\"coord\": [63, 525, 1615, 1173], \"page_id\": 80}], \"