{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775350263-TxfPE3xqWirr03PRA2QX","role":"assistant","created":1775350273,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Looking at the manifest, it seems the data is combined from multiple Treasury Bulletins (January 1970, January 1971, etc.) all into a single JSON file. Let me try to find all the January figures in the JSON file.\n\nLet me look for tables that have \"Total outstanding\" and also include January figures for different years. Since the file seems to contain data for multiple bulletins, I should search through the entire file for patterns like \"1970-January\", \"1971-January\", etc.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_46a2e0c72dbfe3ab","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 -c \"\nimport json\nimport re\n\nwith open('/app/resources/treasury_bulletin_1969_10.json', 'r') as f:\n    data = json.load(f)\n\n# Look for all January data in tables with Total outstanding \nall_january = []\n\nfor elem in data['document']['elements']:\n    if elem.get('type') == 'table':\n        content = elem.get('content', '')\n        \n        # Look for various January patterns in the debt tables\n        # Pattern: Year-Month or Year - Month\n        patterns = [\n            r'<tr><td>(\\d{4}-January[^<]*)</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>',\n            r'<tr><td>(\\d{4} - January[^<]*)</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>',\n            r'<tr><td>(January \\d{4})</td><td>([0-9,]+)</td>',\n        ]\n        \n        for pattern in patterns:\n            matches = re.findall(pattern, content)\n            for m in matches:\n                all_january.append((m[0], m[1], content[:200]))\n\n# Print unique January entries\nfor entry in sorted(set(all_january)):\n    print(f'{entry[0]}: {entry[1]}')\n\""}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
